From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@loudthinking.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur: Restrict cluster_cl5 idle state to
 s2idle

Entering cluster_cl5 during active runtime cpuidle triggers random hard
freezes and spontaneous restarts on Glymur (Snapdragon X2) laptops such
as the ASUS Zenbook A16 (UX3607OA).

However, dropping domain-idle-states = <&cluster_cl5> from cluster0_pd,
cluster1_pd and cluster2_pd orphans domain_ss3 (0x0200c354) in PSCI OSI
mode: during s2idle, CPUs attempt psci_cpu_suspend_enter(0x0200c354)
without any cluster entering cluster_cl5, causing firmware to return
PSCI_RET_DENIED (-1) ~18,600 times per second and breaking s2idle across
all Glymur laptops.

Keep domain-idle-states = <&cluster_cl5> attached to the three CPU
clusters and raise cluster_cl5's min-residency-us to 1000000000 (1000 s)
instead. Runtime cpuidle never selects cluster_cl5 (Usage=0, Rejected=0),
preserving the hard-freeze mitigation, while cpuidle_enter_s2idle()
ignores min-residency-us so s2idle enters cluster_cl5 and domain_ss3
cleanly (reaching full APSS, CXSD, AOSD and DDR collapse).

Closes: https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues/19916
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi	2026-11-27 14:06:19.829799528 +0100
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi	2026-11-27 14:06:19.831044365 +0100
@@ -373,7 +373,7 @@
 				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x01000054>;
 				entry-latency-us = <2000>;
 				exit-latency-us = <2000>;
-				min-residency-us = <9000>;
+				min-residency-us = <1000000000>;
 			};
 
 			domain_ss3: domain-sleep-0 {
